SC2SLR: drop horizontal flip from the training transform, as the paper does

Why: Sec. 4.3 and Table 2 report that horizontal flipping did not improve WER
and was "excluded from the final augmentation scheme"; the Table 3 system
(20.8/21.2 on PHOENIX-2014, equal to Table 2's last row, which has no flip)
was trained without it. The released transform still applies
RandomHorizontalFlip(0.5). This removes only that line.
Applies after sc2slr-2-contrastive-branch.patch.
---
diff --git a/dataset/dataloader_video.py b/dataset/dataloader_video.py
index 9679052..31125df 100644
--- a/dataset/dataloader_video.py
+++ b/dataset/dataloader_video.py
@@ -138,7 +138,6 @@ class BaseFeeder(data.Dataset):
                 # video_augmentation.CenterCrop(224),
                 # video_augmentation.WERAugment('/lustre/wangtao/current_exp/exp/baseline/boundary.npy'),
                 video_augmentation.RandomCrop(self.input_size),
-                video_augmentation.RandomHorizontalFlip(0.5),
                 video_augmentation.Resize(self.image_scale),
                 video_augmentation.ToTensor(),
                 video_augmentation.TemporalRescale(0.2, self.frame_interval),
